# Bavarian (Boarisch) editor and language-server surfaces: the footer, the
# diagnostics panel, the variant picker, the accessibility button and the
# context-help panel. Selected by `uiLocale`.
#
# Translated from `locales/en/editor.ftl`, which is the source of truth.
# Message ids are never translated — only the text to the right of `=`.
#
# UNREVIEWED SEED. Machine-generated, pending review by a speaker (#1521).
# Correct anything here freely; nothing in it was written by a translator.
#
# **Script and orthography.** Latin script, German-based spelling, following
# the **Bavarian Wikipedia (bar.wikipedia)** in its **Central Bavarian /
# Austro-Bavarian** register. **Bavarian has no codified standard** — no
# orthography board, no official dictionary, no agreed norm. **ß is used**,
# unlike `locales/gsw`. See `chrome.ftl` for the full note.
#
# **Do not edit this file toward Standard German**: «ned», «is», «san», «hod»,
# «ko», «koa», «nix», «oda», «Fehla», «Zeiln», «Seitn», «zoagn» are the
# catalog, not typos.
#
# **There is no simple past** in Bavarian — the perfect does all of that work
# — which is why the past-tense sentences here read as perfects: «es san koane
# Verstöß gfundn worn», never a preterite.
#
# **What is borrowed.** The buttons, the connectives and the everyday nouns
# are Bavarian; the editor's technical nouns («Attribut», «Referenz»,
# «Komponentn», «Dokumentation») are Standard German, the register a Bavarian
# speaker is schooled in.
#
# **Counts.** CLDR has **no plural data for `bar`**, so no plural category can
# be selected: this file writes **no** `[zero]`, `[one]`, `[two]`, `[few]` or
# `[many]` branch anywhere. `editor-accessibility-label` and `help-coordinates`
# therefore carry one form each rather than English's singular/plural split.
#
# **Digits.** Every number renders in Latin digits.
#
# **`WCAG`, `WCAG AA`, `DoenetML` and `XML` are names**, not words, and stay in
# English exactly as `locales/en` writes them. So do the DoenetML identifiers
# `styleNumber` and the attribute names in `help-reset-overrides`. Every
# symbolic selector — `$action`, `$status`, `$shortcut`, `$reason`,
# `$location`, `$allowed`, `$line`, `$perItem` — is kept byte for byte from
# English.


## The viewer's controls

editor-update-viewer =
    { $action ->
        [reset] Zrucksetzn
       *[update] Aktualisian
    }

# Bavarian puts the verb last, so the word arrives after the noun it acts on,
# the same shape `locales/de` and `locales/gsw` use.
editor-update-viewer-title =
    { $shortcut ->
        [none] D Ozeig { $word }
       *[other] D Ozeig { $word } { $shortcut }
    }


